{% extends '@layout/default.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Implementing Time-based One-Time Password (TOTP) in Dotkernel{% endblock %}

{% block page_title %}
    <div class="mb-2 text-uppercase small fw-bold text-primary tracking-wider">Headless Platform</div>
    <h1 class="fw-bold text-dark display-6 mb-0">Implementing Time-based One-Time Password (TOTP) in Dotkernel</h1>
    <hr class="mt-4 mb-2 opacity-25">
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="user-content-what-totp-does">What TOTP Does<a href="#what-totp-does"></a></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A <strong>Time-based One-Time Password (TOTP)</strong> is a security algorithm used as part of <strong>two-factor authentication (2FA)</strong> to protect against account attacks. The mechanism is integrated into <a href="https://github.com/dotkernel/dot-totp" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank">dot-totp</a> to enhance security by requiring both a <strong>password</strong> and <strong>an additional one-time code</strong>. Our implementation follows the industry standard of using an Authenticator app to generate temporary, unique 6 digit codes that change every 30 seconds.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In this article we will:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class="wp-block-list"><!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>Install <code>dot-totp</code> in <a href="https://github.com/dotkernel/admin" data-type="link" data-id="https://github.com/dotkernel/admin" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Dotkernel Admin</a>.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>Review how <code>dot-totp</code> behaves in the UI.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You can also follow the installation steps in our <a href="https://docs.dotkernel.org/admin-documentation/v7/tutorials/install-dot-totp/" data-type="link" data-id="https://docs.dotkernel.org/admin-documentation/v7/tutorials/install-dot-totp/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">documentation site</a>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="user-content-2fa-with-totp-flow">2FA with TOTP Flow<a href="#2fa-with-totp-flow"></a></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Below is a simplified flow for the 2FA with TOTP mechanism.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":8613,"sizeSlug":"full","linkDestination":"none"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img src="https://www.dotkernel.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/totp-flow.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-8613"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="user-content-how-to-install-dot-totp">How to Install dot-totp<a href="#how-to-install-dot-totp"></a></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you haven't already, install <a href="https://github.com/dotkernel/admin" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank">Dotkernel Admin</a>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>These installation steps should work similarly in any middleware-based application.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The first step is to include the package into your project by running this command:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:enlighter/codeblock {"language":"shell"} -->
<pre class="EnlighterJSRAW" data-enlighter-language="shell" data-enlighter-theme="" data-enlighter-highlight="" data-enlighter-linenumbers="" data-enlighter-lineoffset="" data-enlighter-title="" data-enlighter-group="">composer require dotkernel/dot-totp</pre>
<!-- /wp:enlighter/codeblock -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>We will follow the Dotkernel file structure and create the files in the list below. If you follow the links from the <a href="https://github.com/dotkernel/admin-documentation/tree/main/code_examples/totp" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank">main totp integration example</a>, you can download the files and add them to your codebase.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class="wp-block-list"><!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><a href="https://github.com/dotkernel/admin-documentation/tree/main/code_examples/totp/src/Admin/src/Form/RecoveryForm.php" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">src/Admin/src/Form/RecoveryForm.php</a></li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><a href="https://github.com/dotkernel/admin-documentation/tree/main/code_examples/totp/src/Admin/src/Form/TotpForm.php" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">src/Admin/src/Form/TotpForm.php</a></li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><a href="https://github.com/dotkernel/admin-documentation/tree/main/code_examples/totp/src/Admin/src/Handler/Account/GetDisableTotpFormHandler.php" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">src/Admin/src/Handler/Account/GetDisableTotpFormHandler.php</a></li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><a href="https://github.com/dotkernel/admin-documentation/tree/main/code_examples/totp/src/Admin/src/Handler/Account/GetEnableTotpFormHandler.php" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">src/Admin/src/Handler/Account/GetEnableTotpFormHandler.php</a></li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><a href="https://github.com/dotkernel/admin-documentation/tree/main/code_examples/totp/src/Admin/src/Handler/Account/GetRecoveryFormHandler.php" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">src/Admin/src/Handler/Account/GetRecoveryFormHandler.php</a></li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><a href="https://github.com/dotkernel/admin-documentation/tree/main/code_examples/totp/src/Admin/src/Handler/Account/GetTotpHandler.php" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">src/Admin/src/Handler/Account/GetTotpHandler.php</a></li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><a href="https://github.com/dotkernel/admin-documentation/tree/main/code_examples/totp/src/Admin/src/Handler/Account/PostDisableTotpHandler.php" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">src/Admin/src/Handler/Account/PostDisableTotpHandler.php</a></li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><a href="https://github.com/dotkernel/admin-documentation/tree/main/code_examples/totp/src/Admin/src/Handler/Account/PostEnableTotpHandler.php" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">src/Admin/src/Handler/Account/PostEnableTotpHandler.php</a></li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><a href="https://github.com/dotkernel/admin-documentation/tree/main/code_examples/totp/src/Admin/src/Handler/Account/PostValidateRecoveryHandler.php" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">src/Admin/src/Handler/Account/PostValidateRecoveryHandler.php</a></li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><a href="https://github.com/dotkernel/admin-documentation/tree/main/code_examples/totp/src/Admin/src/Handler/Account/PostValidateTotpHandler.php" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">src/Admin/src/Handler/Account/PostValidateTotpHandler.php</a></li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><a href="https://github.com/dotkernel/admin-documentation/tree/main/code_examples/totp/src/Admin/templates/admin/recovery-form.html.twig" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">src/Admin/templates/admin/recovery-form.html.twig</a></li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><a href="https://github.com/dotkernel/admin-documentation/tree/main/code_examples/totp/src/App/src/Middleware/CancelUrlMiddleware.php" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">src/App/src/Middleware/CancelUrlMiddleware.php</a></li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><a href="https://github.com/dotkernel/admin-documentation/tree/main/code_examples/totp/src/App/src/Middleware/TotpMiddleware.php" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">src/App/src/Middleware/TotpMiddleware.php</a></li>
<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You can use the trait at <a href="https://github.com/dotkernel/admin-documentation/tree/main/code_examples/totp/src/Core/src/App/src/Entity/TotpTrait.php" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank">src/Core/src/App/src/Entity/TotpTrait.php</a> in any entity where you need 2FA.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Make sure to migrate the new columns <code>totpSecret</code>, <code>totp_enabled</code> and <code>recovery_codes</code> in your entity.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>There are still some code snippets in the <a href="https://github.com/dotkernel/admin-documentation/tree/main/code_examples/totp" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank">_misc</a> folder:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class="wp-block-list"><!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><a href="https://github.com/dotkernel/admin-documentation/tree/main/code_examples/totp/_misc/totp-append-view-account.html.twig" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">The enable/disable 2FA button</a> should be used in the <code>view-account.html.twig</code> file or in a new page.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><a href="https://github.com/dotkernel/admin-documentation/tree/main/code_examples/totp/_misc/totp-append-routes.php" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">The routes updates</a> must be added in the <code>src/Admin/src/RoutesDelegator.php</code> file.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><a href="https://github.com/dotkernel/admin-documentation/tree/main/code_examples/totp/_misc/totp-append-Pipeline.php" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">The pipeline updates</a> must be added in the <code>config/pipeline.php</code> file after <code>$app-&gt;pipe(AuthMiddleware::class);</code>.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><a href="https://github.com/dotkernel/admin-documentation/tree/main/code_examples/totp/_misc/totp-append-ConfigProvider.php" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">The ConfigProvider updates</a> must be added in the <code>src/Admin/src/ConfigProvider.php</code> file.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="user-content-dot-totp-in-action">dot-totp in Action</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Once you have <code>dot-totp</code> implemented, you can activate the feature in your admin accounts. If you navigate to your profile from the top-right image in Dotkernel Admin, you should see this box.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":8615,"sizeSlug":"full","linkDestination":"custom"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img src="https://www.dotkernel.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/profile-totp-deactivated.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-8615"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Simply click on 'Enable TOTP' to begin the activation process.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>We blurred out the QR code and recovery codes for this tutorial. You will receive dynamically generated versions that will be fully visible to you.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You will need to have an Authenticator app installed on your mobile device.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":8616,"sizeSlug":"full","linkDestination":"custom"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img src="https://www.dotkernel.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/totp-activate-qr.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-8616"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Follow the instructions on the screen:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class="wp-block-list"><!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>Scan the QR code with your mobile device.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>Enter the 6-digit code it generates on your mobile device.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The code refreshes every 30 seconds.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The TOPT activation flow will list several recovery codes you can use if your mobile device isn't available.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":8618,"sizeSlug":"full","linkDestination":"custom"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img src="https://www.dotkernel.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/totp-recovery-codes.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-8618"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Each recovery code is usable only once.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Save the recovery codes in a secure location.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If the code is valid, you will be logged in, and TOTP will be activated for your account.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Whenever you need to log into the account, you will start by entering your username and password, like before. Since TOTP is activated, you will need to also submit the code from your Authenticator app. Alternatively, you can submit a recovery code.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":8617,"sizeSlug":"full","linkDestination":"custom"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img src="https://www.dotkernel.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/totp-ask-code.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-8617"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>That's it! You are now logged in securely.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

